ns/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:402:# 3. Compute treeness/RCV ON THE FILTERED SET\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:426:The bundled `scogs_paired_compare.py --metric long_branch_score\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:434:### Treeness/RCV: use the right input file\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:436:`phykit toverr` (a.k.a. `treeness_over_rcv`) takes BOTH alignment and tree. Use the **trimmed** alignment (`*.faa.mafft.clipkit`) paired with its **treefile** (`*.faa.mafft.clipkit.treefile`), not the raw `.faa.mafft`. ClipKit-trimmed alignments are what produced the canonical tree, so the RCV must be computed on the same trimmed alignment for the ratio to match published numbers.\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:443:### Treeness (RCV ratio)\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:448:- `phykit treeness <tree_file>` — outputs treeness (RCV) value\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/SKILL.md:460:  --dir scogs_fungi --function treeness --ext .treefile --stat median\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/QUICK_START.md:7:## scogs animal-vs-fungi questions — START HERE\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/QUICK_START.md:9:When the data folder has `scogs_animals.zip` and/or `scogs_fungi.zip`,\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/QUICK_START.md:11:ortholog for BOTH groups, plus Mann-Whitney U + p-value, paired\n/workspace/tmp/tu/ToolUniverse-main/plugins/tooluniverse/skills/tooluniverse-phylogenetics/QUICK_STA